From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 07:37:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PhoneSwitcher: notify the active data sub whenever it changes

On a single SIM device whose radio has no setPreferredDataModem,
mHalCommandToUse is HAL_COMMAND_ALLOW_DATA and sendRilCommands guards its
only work with mActiveModemCount > 1. Nothing is sent, the Message is never
delivered, EVENT_MODEM_COMMAND_DONE never arrives, and the diffDetected path
never notifies. The only other notify was an else-if that required the subId
to change in an evaluation where the phoneId did not, and at first boot both
change together, so it is missed permanently.

TelephonyRegistry therefore keeps mActiveDataSubId=-1 for the life of the
boot. Measured on a vs995: data connected and validated, PhoneSwitcher
looping 'activate 0', notifyPreferredDataSubIdChanged never once logged, and
SystemUI holding showExclamation=true because it cannot resolve
isDefaultDataEnabled without an active data sub. The user sees a permanent
error mark on a working LTE icon.

Notifying on any subId change is the smaller claim and matches what every
consumer of getActiveDataSubscriptionId expects.
---
 .../telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java         | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
index 6d2e77d643..4bec69af2a 100644
--- a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/data/PhoneSwitcher.java
@@ -1152,8 +1152,23 @@ public class PhoneSwitcher extends Handler {
             sb.append(" preferred data phoneId ").append(oldPreferredDataPhoneId)
                     .append("->").append(mPreferredDataPhoneId);
             diffDetected = true;
-        } else if (oldPreferredDataSubId != mPreferredDataSubId.get()) {
-            logl("SIM refresh, notify dds change");
+        }
+
+        // Notify whenever the subId actually changed, not only when the phoneId held still.
+        //
+        // The else-if this replaces assumed the diffDetected path would notify later, off the
+        // EVENT_MODEM_COMMAND_DONE reply. On a single SIM device whose radio has no
+        // setPreferredDataModem, mHalCommandToUse is HAL_COMMAND_ALLOW_DATA and sendRilCommands
+        // guards its only work with `mActiveModemCount > 1`, so no command is ever sent, the
+        // Message is never delivered and that reply never arrives. At first boot the phoneId and
+        // the subId change in the same evaluation, diffDetected wins, and the notification is
+        // missed for good: every later evaluation sees both values unchanged.
+        //
+        // TelephonyRegistry then keeps mActiveDataSubId=-1 forever. Data works, but anything
+        // reading getActiveDataSubscriptionId sees no active data sub, and SystemUI cannot resolve
+        // isDefaultDataEnabled, so it draws the error exclamation over a perfectly good LTE icon.
+        if (oldPreferredDataSubId != mPreferredDataSubId.get()) {
+            logl("notify dds change " + oldPreferredDataSubId + "->" + mPreferredDataSubId.get());
             // Inform connectivity about the active data phone
             notifyPreferredDataSubIdChanged();
         }
